    {
      "id": "586953dc-a2af-45cc-8eff-f6d5441f6ece",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 11,
      "shortName": "regression-widget-glow-only-on",
      "title": "REGRESSION: widget glow only on focused elements (lost rest-state glow)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Reported by user 2026-07-16. SYMPTOM: changing the glow-size Select no longer visibly affects widgets at rest; glow appears only on focused/hovered elements.\n\n## DIAGNOSIS (code archaeology — original hypothesis FALSIFIED)\nNo regression event exists: widget glow conditions AND values byte-identical since pre-refactor baseline 833c214; scaled_glow chokepoint, showcase wiring, renderer path all correct. TRUTH: most control surfaces never passed a REST glow — glow was a hover/on/checked affordance — so glow_size had almost nothing to scale at rest.\n\n## FIX (user direction: theme owns the glow COLOR, the config glow_size setting owns the amount, honored by ALL widgets at widget-base level)\n- Theme token `interaction.control_rest_glow: u8` (default 30 ≈ 0.12; 0 = flat; serde-default) + BASE-LEVEL `PaintCx::rest_glow(radius)` (component.rs, beside scaled_glow): color from theme.colors.glow, intensity from the token; runs through scaled_glow so glow_size (none/thin/medium/large) scales presence+radius+strength uniformly.\n- Wired at rest: Button Primary/Destructive/Outline, Input, Toggle track, Checkbox BOX, Select trigger, Pane (all variants), DockFrame fill, Tag (toned), Alert (toned).\n\n## ROUND 3 (2026-07-17, from user's first GPU pass) — uncommitted, awaiting final verification\nUser findings + fixes:\n1. \"Button glow too much vs other widgets\" → new REST_GLOW_RADIUS = 12 for the resting base rect (the hover halo keeps GLOW_RADIUS 30); Outline lerps radius rest→hover with p.\n2. \"Toasts have no glow\" → Toast card surface now carries the rest glow, toned to its severity.\n3. \"Icons no glow\" → NOT POSSIBLE at the widget level: an Icon is a glyph text run (TextCmd) and glow is an SDF RECT renderer feature — a glyph halo needs a renderer capability (SDF text/glyph glow). RECORDED as a follow-up (renderer feature), documented in widgets.md; not faked with rects. RailCell's bare-icon rest state is flat for the same reason (by design).\n4. \"ScrollRegion no glow (probably correct?)\" → frameless region: CORRECT (no surface). A STYLED region (.background/.border scrollable panel) now falls back to the rest glow when no explicit .glow set.\n5. \"Not all chrome elements have glow\" → FILLED Row (the list/pane cards, e.g. showcase PANES) now falls back to the rest glow; unfilled Row/Item rows, ChromeRegion (layout shell) and RailCell rest stay deliberately flat (no surface). DockFrame fill was already wired in round 2.\nFocus batch (T014) verified \"Perfect\" by user; regression glance \"looks good\".\n- Docs: widgets.md consolidated \"The glow model — who owns what\" + \"The focus model — ring visibility\" sections (TOC updated) on top of the per-widget notes; config.default.toml glow_size/show_focus_border comments.\n- Workspace green, clippy clean. Single commit with the focus work per user request.\n\nVERIFY (user, GPU showcase): button rest halo now matches other controls; toasts (t) halo in their severity tone; pane cards in the chrome demo halo; the styled two-axis ScrollRegion demo halos; GLOW select none→large scales all of it; icons still flat (renderer follow-up).\n\n## FOLLOW-UP (recorded, out of scope here): SDF glyph/text glow renderer capability so Icon (and RailCell's bare-icon rest) can halo.",
      "notes": "",
