    {
      "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 12,
      "shortName": "scrollregion-keyboard-scroll-a",
      "title": "ScrollRegion keyboard-scroll actions (prefix+Home/End/PgUp/PgDown; horizontal trigger TBD)",
      "status": "blocked",
      "description": "USER-CORRECTED DECISION (2026-07-16): NEW app-side actions driving a ScrollRegion from the keyboard — vertical prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown.\n\nUSER DECISION 2026-07-17 (horizontal trigger — SETTLED): create a HORIZONTAL scroll Action, default prefix+Shift+PageUp / prefix+Shift+PageDown (page-left / page-right). No collision with prefix+Shift+ArrowLeft/Right (niri view pan) nor terminal scrollback Shift+ bindings.\n\n═══ ⛔ BLOCKED ON A CROSS-FEATURE DEPENDENCY (registered 2026-07-17) ═══\nThe unblock work does NOT live in this phase. It lives in **F004 (📐 Grid-UI Widget Library) / P001 (gridui-01: Scroll/list primitive)** — note that PHASE F004/P001 is itself currently `deferred`:\n\n- **F004/P001/T006 — \"Sidebar scroll wire to ScrollRegion\" [planned] = THE HARD BLOCKER.**\n  Mounts the sidebar workspace tree inside a ScrollRegion (+ SidebarNav cursor calls ensure_visible). This creates the FIRST app-side ScrollRegion for T012's actions to target. Files: heca/src/sidebar/*, heca/src/chrome/*. Overlaps plugin-03 (= F003/P004, DONE).\n- **F004/P001/T007 — \"Scrollable region pick mode\" [planned] = ALTERNATIVE ROUTING ANSWER.**\n  prefix+<key> → KeyHint overlay enumerating every scrollable region → pick → sticky scroll mode (WmAction::ScrollFocused). A THIRD answer to T012's routing question (vs focused / hovered). Backlog says: run /grill-me FIRST (key choice, sticky vs one-shot, pick→focus vs pick→mode). Only needed once multiple regions compete for j/k.\n- **F004/P001/T002 — \"PageUp and PageDown scroll keys\" [deferred] = LIKELY PREREQUISITE.**\n  VERIFIED 2026-07-17: `GridKey` (heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs ~line 265) has `Home`/`End` but NO `PageUp`/`PageDown`. It was deferred for \"no consumer\" — the user's prefix+(Shift+)PageUp/PageDown decision GIVES it a consumer. Needed if the scroll intent reaches the widget as a key; NOT needed if it arrives as a semantic WidgetIntent or a direct imperative call (preferred).\n- F004/P001/T001 (ScrollRegion core) = done. T003/T004 canceled, T005 (nested wheel hit-testing) deferred.\n\n═══ WHY BLOCKED (verified in code 2026-07-17) ═══\n- NO chrome surface mounts a grid-ui ScrollRegion. Verified: `ScrollRegion` appears in heca/src ONLY in chrome/realize.rs (the WidgetKind::Scroll mapper arm + doc comments) — 5 hits, all mapper/docs. The only LIVE ScrollRegion is in the showcase (heca-renderer example), a separate binary the WmAction system cannot reach (crate layering: WmAction/KeymapRegistry/ActionRegistry/RPC live in the top-level `heca` app crate; the showcase is a bottom-level heca-renderer example that cannot depend on the app).\n- Existing scroll handlers drive the TERMINAL/WORKSPACE, not a ScrollRegion (handlers.rs: handle_scroll_page_up→backend.scroll_viewport_animated; scroll_view_by→ws.scrolling.scroll_view).\n- No keyboard→widget-tree routing for chrome: chrome trees receive POINTER events only; the sole Event::Widget dispatch in heca is realize.rs test code (Tabs).\n⇒ Landing the WmActions + default binds now = DEAD keybindings occupying prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown (+Shift). Violates AGENTS.md ⛔ rule 3 (\"no for-now fixes\") and shadows keys user-visibly.\n\n═══ ROUTING DESIGN (agent decision 2026-07-17, confirm on return) ═══\nTarget = the ScrollRegion on the currently FOCUSED chrome surface; else NO-OP (never fall back to terminal scrollback). Mirrors the existing focus/overlay routing model, no hovered-region mouse tracking. NOTE: F004/P001/T007 proposes a different model (explicit pick → sticky mode) — decide between them before building.\nScrollRegion API to drive (exists + tested): scroll_to()/scroll_offset() (vertical), scroll_to_x()/scroll_offset_x() (horizontal), ensure_visible(), scroll_to_child().\n\n═══ UNBLOCK PATH (in order) ═══\n1. F004/P001/T006 (sidebar ScrollRegion mount) — the real unblock.\n2. Settle routing: focused-surface (this task's decision) vs F004/P001/T007 pick-mode. /grill-me if taking T007.\n3. Focused-surface scroll-intent routing path (new WidgetIntent::Scroll* variants, or imperative call).\n4. THEN the FULL Adding-New-Actions checklist (AGENTS.md): WmAction variants → action_from_name → action_priority → action_policy() (exhaustive) → handler → build_registry → keybindings.default.toml (vertical prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown; horizontal prefix+Shift+PageUp/PageDown) → ActionRegistry::ALL descriptor → rpc.rs → README. Configurable via KeymapRegistry, never hardcoded.\n5. USER verifies in the GPU showcase.\n\nRule: capability reachable from mouse (scrollbar) + keybinding/action + RPC. Per-axis availability (vertical-only region ignores horizontal). Clamp handled by the widget. Edge case: action fired with no ScrollRegion on the active surface → no-op (no panic, no scrollback fallback).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-001-planned-blocked",
