    {
      "id": "b413c466-8239-4787-94f3-b1623d041aad",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 14,
      "shortName": "overlay-follow-ups-anchor-to-r",
      "title": "Overlay follow-ups: anchor-to-rect mode + convert Select/Tooltip/ContextMenu/CommandPalette panels; overlay sizing + scrollable modal body; SDF glyph glow",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "Follow-up scope deferred out of T009 (base Overlay + BUG A, d448702) and T011 (rest glow, 7ff3b59).\n\n⚠️ SCOPE SPLIT 2026-07-24 — two remaining chunks moved to their own tasks so they are trackable:\n- **F003/P011/T015** — Overlay sizing (.panel_size) + scrollable modal body.\n- **F003/P011/T016** — SDF glyph/text glow renderer (Icon + RailCell rest glow). Renderer work, not grid-ui widgets.\nWhat REMAINS in T014 = the panel conversions + the Tooltip decision (below).\n\n═══ STEP 1 — PLACEMENT AUTHORITY: COMMITTED da5961d + USER-VERIFIED ═══\noverlay.rs: `place_anchored(anchor_rect, panel, viewport, gap)` (rect-anchored) + `place_at_point(anchor_point, panel, viewport, inset, centered)` (point-anchored) + `OverlayPosition { Center (default) | Anchored }` with `.position()`/`.anchored()`/`.set_anchor()` (placement baked into the panel child on layout via shift_subtree, idempotent). ContextMenu::layout() delegates to `place_at_point`. Planner state a43e2c1.\n\n═══ STEP 2 — SELECT: COMMITTED d14c24d + USER-VERIFIED (\"now looks good\") ═══\n2a. `panel_top()` removed; `panel_rect()` → `place_anchored_on(...)`. NEW `AnchorSide { Auto | Below | Above }` so a caller can pass a side it already decided — load-bearing: Select's flip decision and its visible-row COUNT are computed together in open_list() (panel height depends on the side).\n2b. NEW `paint_panel_chrome(cx, rect, PanelChrome { border, glow })`. `Overlay::paint` uses it (inline copy deleted); Select passes its accent border + glow.\n- Rows remain PLACED CHILDREN of Select; `bounds === drawn === clickable` and `choice_at` untouched — that is WHY Select paints the panel itself rather than composing an `Overlay`.\n\n⚠️ BUG INTRODUCED AND FIXED IN STEP 2 — READ BEFORE TOUCHING ANY PANEL RECT:\nAn interim version clamped Select's panel against the viewport cached during paint. `panel_rect()` is computed TWICE per frame — by `place_options()` (layout, to place the rows) and by `paint()` — so ANY time-varying input makes them disagree and the rows visibly DETACH from the panel. Symptoms: tall list (negative y snapped to 0) → rows outside the panel; Select near the right edge (x clamped) → row content on the border. FIX: `panel_rect()` is a PURE function of bounds + side + row heights (infinite viewport passed deliberately); on-screen fit is kept by capping the visible row COUNT in `open_list()`. Regression tests: `open_panel_rect_is_independent_of_the_cached_viewport`, `flipped_panel_is_not_clamped_even_when_it_overflows_the_top`.\n\n═══ STEP 3 — DOCS: COMMITTED 742cf5f, 98fd6a5 ═══\ndocs/widgets.md §Overlay \"Implementing an overlay-panel widget\": path A (compose an Overlay), path B (paint it yourself but reuse the authorities — sketched as `MySelect`, a cut-down of the real Select), the ⚠️ pure-rect invariant, and a \"which authority to call\" table.\n\n═══ STEP 4 — CONTEXTMENU + COMMANDPALETTE + THE FRAME SETTING: COMMITTED fa4dab8, 1260226, 0388296, 5913787 + USER-VERIFIED (\"to me it look ok now\") ═══\n- context_menu.rs + command_palette.rs call `paint_panel_chrome` (same tokens ⇒ fill/radius/border/glow unchanged). Palette's scrim untouched (a blocking layer's scrim is not panel chrome). ⇒ ALL FOUR overlay panels (Overlay/Dialog, Select, ContextMenu, CommandPalette) share ONE chrome implementation; `FrameStyle::` is matched in exactly one place (overlay.rs) — verified by grep, no widget branches on it.\n- The bracket reticle was HARDCODED there. Now a policy decision (memory: use existing policy systems, never hardcode):\n  · heca-theme: NEW `FrameStyle { None | Bordered | Bracketed }` + `colors.overlay_frame` (default Bracketed). Lives in the THEME crate because heca-grid-ui reads it at paint time and cannot depend on heca-config — the same path `show_focus_border` takes.\n  · heca-config: `[appearance] overlay_border_style` + `effective_overlay_border_style()` + `From<BorderStyle> for FrameStyle` (reuses the EXISTING user-facing enum).\n  · heca: applied in `chrome_gui_theme` next to show_focus_border ⇒ live-reloads.\n  · `FrameStyle` exported from grid-ui root + prelude.\n- SHOWCASE does NOT read config.toml (own Theme from heca_theme::load_theme + font defaults) ⇒ added an **OVERLAY FRAME** select writing the same `theme.colors.overlay_frame` token (1260226).\n- SHADOW raised on user feedback: SHADOW_BLUR_MULT 4.0→6.0, SHADOW_DROP 12.0→16.0 (two consts atop overlay.rs).\n- ⚠️ BUG FOUND BY USER AND FIXED (0388296): `overlay_frame` governed only the RETICLE while `chrome.border` was drawn unconditionally, so NONE left the accent border on screen. Now it owns the WHOLE edge — Bracketed = edge+reticle, Bordered = edge only, None = NO edge. `PanelChrome.border` reinterpreted as the widget's preferred edge COLOUR (ignored under None; theme's neutral border fills in when a widget supplies none). Fill + glow never suppressed (the halo is identity, not a frame). Two tests count bordered draw commands to lock the policy.\n- Also fixed a PRE-EXISTING red test: T011 raised `GlowLevel::Thin.strength_scale()` 0.5→0.75 but left the assertion at 0.5 ⇒ heca-theme was failing on HEAD.\n- Docs: config.default.toml + README + docs/widgets.md (edge-policy table).\n- Workspace 863 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n═══ REMAINING IN T014 ═══\n1. **Tooltip — DECISION, then act.** It is a transparent HOVER wrapper (4-side centered bubble, no open_signal, no input capture, `damage_bounds` unions the bubble). Its bubble is deliberately lighter/smaller than a panel, so the shared drop shadow (dy 16, blur ×6) + bracket reticle are very likely WRONG for it. Leaning: LEAVE its chrome alone — a tooltip is not a panel — and do NOT unify placement either, because its 4-side flip/clamp (`bubble_rect`, tooltip.rs:165-196) differs in kind from the dropdown below/above rule; a `place_beside(rect, panel, vp, gap, side)` authority is only worth adding when a SECOND consumer needs it (YAGNI). Confirm with the user, record the decision here, and close this item either way — do not leave it dangling.\n2. Nothing else — sizing → T015, glyph glow → T016.\n\nEDGE CASES: nested anchored overlays; corners; blocking vs light-dismiss occlusion must follow the mode.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "2026-07-16T23:01:57.788Z",
