    {
      "id": "bb22b786-77f8-4e23-ae65-f11c5c0a6c58",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 15,
      "shortName": "overlay-sizing-panel-size-scro",
      "title": "Overlay sizing (.panel_size) + scrollable modal body",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "Split out of T014 (2026-07-24). Original T009 scope gap; builds on the placement + panel-chrome authorities T014 delivered.\n\n═══ COMMITTED f2f65de (2026-07-24) — awaiting final user re-test ═══\n`Overlay::panel_size(width, height)` + `Dialog::panel_size(..)`. Order-independent (stored on the Overlay and re-applied when `panel()`/`panel_boxed()` replaces the child), opt-in (unset = hug content). `Length::Pct` resolves against the VIEWPORT (the Overlay fills it); `Px` pins.\n\nWHY THE TWO HALVES ARE ONE FEATURE: a ScrollRegion only scrolls when its parent BOUNDS it. An unsized panel grows with its content, so nothing overflows and no scrollbar appears.\n\n═══ FOUR BUGS FOUND WHILE VERIFYING — all fixed in the WIDGETS, not pushed onto callers ═══\n1. **ScrollRegion could not shrink below its content** ⇒ it overflowed its parent instead of scrolling (user: \"content still overflow the modal, it should show scrollbars\"). TWO causes, both in `Style`: (a) no `min_size` mapping at all, so taffy used its default `min: auto` = the item's CONTENT size; (b) a blanket `flex_shrink: 0.0` (\"never let a flex container squish widgets\"). FIX: `Style` gains `min_width`/`min_height`/`max_width`/`max_height` (Option<Length>) + `flex_shrink: Option<f32>` (None ⇒ 0.0, preserving the old rule); `ScrollRegion::new()` sets min 0 / shrink 1 ON ITSELF — being smaller than its content is what a viewport IS, not a caller setting.\n2. **Panel could exceed the window** and get cut by the screen edge (user: \"modal bigger than the main window\"). FIX: `Overlay::apply_panel_size` now ALWAYS caps the panel at `Pct(1.0)` (unconditional, not only when panel_size is set), and the Overlay carries `padding = VIEWPORT_MARGIN (24.0)` so the cap resolves against an inset content box ⇒ a maxed panel keeps a margin instead of having its border/glow shaved (user: \"should leave a little margin around\").\n3. **Wheel never reached a ScrollRegion inside a modal; thumb drag stuck to the cursor** (user: \"Wheel not works. When click and drag mouse cannot be released anymore\"). CAUSE: `Dialog::event` and `Overlay::event` only offered `Scroll` to `overlay_active` descendants (a ScrollRegion is NOT one) and neither routed `PointerReleased` AT ALL (it fell to the `_ => Handled::No` catch-all), so the grab never ended. FIX: both route Scroll to the panel first (then the modal swallow keeps the page behind still) and route PointerReleased to the panel.\n4. **Rows cut on the left** (user-reported twice). CAUSE: ScrollRegion clipped to EXACTLY its bounds, but every bordered surface paints a rest-glow halo OUTSIDE its own bounds (T011) ⇒ a child flush against the edge had its halo scissored. FIX: widen the clip by GLOW_BLEED on an axis the region does NOT scroll — only the scrolling axis needs a tight cut. Plus default `padding_y` + row `gap` inside the region (user: \"internal children should have more y margin around\").\n\nCALLER BURDEN REMOVED (user: \"this should be internal calculation not something developers or agents should be setting on every modal\"): `Dialog::body()`/`body_boxed()` call `fit_body()`, which fills the panel width and takes the leftover height — only when the caller left them at defaults. So the whole caller side is now:\n    Dialog::new(t).panel_size(Px(560), Px(420)).body(ScrollRegion::new().child(..)).action(..)\n\nMEASURED (probe, viewport 2000x1400, panel 560x420): panel = 560x420 exactly; ScrollRegion child = 524x300 (bounded, gets the leftover); action row inside the panel. Sizing/bounding verified numerically, not by eye.\n\nTESTS: `panel_size_applies_regardless_of_builder_order`, `panel_size_is_opt_in`, `panel_never_exceeds_the_viewport` (asks 4000x3000 in an 800x600 viewport), and `a_sized_panel_bounds_a_scrollable_body` (12-row body in a 300px panel is bounded; the SAME body unsized makes the panel taller — pins the causal claim). Workspace 867 green, clippy clean.\nSHOWCASE: the existing \"Delete pane?\" dialog is the demo — sized panel + scrollable body + the nested Select (T009 BUG A case) in one.\n\nUSER FEEDBACK RESOLVED: dialog should NOT be viewport-proportional ⇒ the demo uses Px; Pct stays available for genuinely modal/proportional overlays.\n\n═══ REMAINING ═══\n- Final user re-test of the four fixes in the GPU showcase (last report was mid-fix: scrollbar appeared, margin + cut-left + stuck-drag still open at that point).\n- Docs: docs/widgets.md §Overlay (Sizing bullet) + §Dialog (scrollable-body recipe) are written; add the `min/max/flex_shrink` Style fields to any Style reference if one exists.\n- NOTE: scrollbar behaviour itself is reimplemented across four widgets — tracked separately as **F004/P001/T008** (audit in that task).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "2026-07-24T17:26:38.183Z",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T17:25:26.669Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-24T19:21:09.528Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "33f9e6f5-3f69-4849-8bc0-e4cccb111877",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 16,
      "shortName": "sdf-glyph-text-glow-renderer-i",
      "title": "SDF glyph/text glow renderer — Icon + RailCell rest glow",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Split out of T014 (2026-07-24) so it is trackable on its own. USER-REQUESTED follow-up to T011 (rest glow, commits 7ff3b59 + 319a349). This is RENDERER work, not grid-ui widget work — it does not belong in an \"overlay follow-ups\" task.\n\nTHE GAP: T011 gave every bordered SURFACE a faint theme rest glow (`interaction.control_rest_glow` + `PaintCx::rest_glow(radius)`), but a GLYPH cannot carry one. `Icon` draws a TextCmd, and glow exists only in the SDF **rect** renderer (heca-renderer/src/grid.rs) — `TextCmd` has no glow field. So a bare-icon control (`Icon`, and `RailCell`'s bare-icon rest state) is deliberately flat today while every surface around it halos. The user asked for icons to be able to halo.\n\nCURRENT STATE (verify before building — these line numbers are from 2026-07-17 notes):\n- heca-grid-ui/src/scene.rs: `DrawCommand::Text(TextCmd)` carries no glow; `DrawCommand::Rect(RectCmd)` carries `Option<Glow>`.\n- heca-renderer/src/grid.rs: the SDF rect renderer implements glow (falloff radius + intensity, scaled by `GlowLevel::radius_scale()`/`strength_scale()` — heca-theme/src/theme.rs:79-105).\n- Text goes through cosmic-text via `TextRenderer` (heca-renderer/src/text.rs? confirm) — `queue_text(text, x, y, size, color)` / `queue_text_in_box(...)` (AGENTS.md §Gotchas: do not conflate them).\n- heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs draws the glyph; rail_cell.rs has the bare-icon rest state.\n- Glow ownership is SETTLED (T011): the THEME owns the colour (`theme.glow`), the `glow_size` setting owns the AMOUNT via the `scaled_glow` chokepoint. Any glyph glow MUST go through the same chokepoint — do not add a second glow scale.\n\nTO BUILD (design first — pick an approach and record it before coding):\n1. Decide the technique. Options: (a) a glyph HALO PASS — re-render the glyph run offset/blurred underneath itself in the glow colour (cheap, no new pipeline, but blur quality is limited); (b) true SDF text rendering in heca-renderer so glyphs get the same falloff maths as rects (correct, much larger change — cosmic-text rasterises alpha masks, so this likely means an SDF atlas); (c) an offscreen bloom-style pass (overlaps F004/P002/T001 \"offscreen bloom pipeline\" — check before duplicating).\n2. Carry glow on the text path: add a glow field to `TextCmd` (or a sibling command) and honour it in the renderer.\n3. Wire `Icon` to `PaintCx::rest_glow` like the surfaces, and `RailCell`'s bare-icon rest state.\n4. Tests where meaningful (scene-level: the command carries the glow), + showcase demo, + docs BOTH audiences.\n\nEDGE CASES / CONSTRAINTS: must respect `glow_size = none` (no halo at all) and the `scaled_glow` chokepoint; must not regress text rendering perf (glyphs are the hottest path — the terminal draws thousands per frame, so gate the halo to CHROME text/icons, never terminal cell glyphs); HiDPI (f64 logical, f32 at the GPU boundary); the halo must not break the dirty-region/damage model (a glowing glyph damages a larger rect than its text box).\n\nVERIFICATION: fully GPU-gated — user drives `cargo run -p heca-renderer --example showcase`. Unit tests cannot confirm a halo.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
